#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:10
msgid "Scope"
msgstr "Ámbito"

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:12
msgid ""
"This chunk covers 12 ledger application modules, 5,115 lines, and 47,661 "
"measured proxy tokens. All nine bounded pages were read. It includes the "
"extraction router and draft records/projections, exact-profile "
"extract/confirm operations, consent-write custody, confirmation "
"orchestration and ports, and a metadata-only local-reader readiness "
"operation. This is static analysis: no reader, model, persistence "
"adapter, or test suite was executed, and no current legal conclusion is "
"made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:14
msgid "Reading stored evidence into a reviewable draft"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:16
msgid ""
"The application resolves one stored evidence record or attachment ID into"
" in-memory bytes, then routes by content-derived document shape. "
"Structured Facturae, CII, and UBL records use an exact reader without a "
"model; the draft preserves line and rate breakdowns, declared country "
"token, invoice class and findings, then runs deterministic checks. "
"Unrecognized XML is refused rather than sent through PDF or image "
"fallbacks. A text-bearing PDF is transcribed by the PDF text layer, read "
"by deterministic label rules first, and filled by a semantic reader only "
"where the label result is incomplete. Model-unavailable or resource-"
"admission failures preserve a partial label result with machine-readable "
"fallback facts; a text-native document with no useful reader refuses "
"rather than silently escalating to vision. Scan-only PDFs and images use "
"a separate vision transcription stage and then the shared semantic "
"reader. Shape routing and input resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`) Label and "
"model-fill policy "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`) Structured"
" read and document checks "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`) Vision "
"path (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:18
msgid ""
"Draft values remain explicitly provisional: every field is optional, per-"
"field provenance carries origin, grounding, anchor/refusal and role-"
"evidence facts, and deterministic discrepancies are returned for operator"
" review. The public projection is closed and bounded; it includes the "
"structured class retained in a private draft attribute, line breakdowns, "
"provenance, findings and source/review digests, while keeping raw "
"transcription text out of the projection. Provenance invariants "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_records.py`) Draft "
"contract (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_records.py`) "
"Bounded draft projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_operation_dtos.py`) "
"Extraction result payload "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_payloads.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:20
msgid ""
"The registered extract request permits exactly one source and either an "
"on-host read or an explicitly acknowledged off-host provider. The off-"
"host route requires a stored evidence ID, not a bare attachment ID. The "
"worker reads that record's verified source hash, asks the injected "
"consent capability to mint a proof for the chosen provider and fixed "
"surface, and the extraction router checks that the token address equals "
"the content digest of the bytes actually loaded. A mismatch is refused "
"before reader dispatch. If a consent ledger save occurs, paired "
"synchronous hooks enter an irreversible section and mark UNKNOWN before "
"the save; only a confirmed save settles UPDATED. Extract request rules "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_extract_operation.py`) "
"Source binding, minting and projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_extract_operation.py`) "
"Byte/token digest check "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`) Consent "
"write custody "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_consent_custody.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:22
msgid ""
"One composition question remains: the extraction module describes the "
"scan/image vision lane as local, but its registered operation accepts an "
"off-host provider and passes it, with the consent proof, into "
"`transcribe_vision` and the later semantic read. The interface clearly "
"records explicit opt-in and content binding, but this slice alone does "
"not establish which stage(s) may use the selected provider or how those "
"dispatches appear in the consent ledger. Verify the concrete adapters "
"preserve provider choice and audit both stages; this is a "
"routing/completeness question, not evidence of a consent bypass. Vision "
"dispatch inputs "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`) Port "
"signatures "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction_ports.py`) "
"Optional off-host capability policy "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:24
msgid "Confirmation and persistence"
msgstr "Confirmación y persistencia"

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:26
msgid ""
"Confirmation is a prepare/build/persist flow. Prepare re-extracts the "
"selected bytes, re-runs the direction and review checks, resolves "
"counterparty establishment and dated authorities, and refuses when the "
"current source digest or complete draft review digest differs from the "
"operator's reviewed values. The registered confirm request requires both "
"digests, exactly one source reference, explicit direction, bounded "
"override fields and individual finding resolutions. The draft digest uses"
" the public projection, which includes the structured invoice class that "
"would otherwise be omitted by a bare model dump. Preparation and "
"source/draft freshness "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) Review digest "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) Confirm "
"request "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_confirm_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:28
msgid ""
"Build layers supplied operator answers over recovered values, refuses "
"missing required identity/number/date/base data, checks "
"filer/counterparty identity constraints, retains structured lines when "
"amounts were not restated, and delegates invoice construction to the "
"canonical catalogue writer. Confirmation first checks whether the same "
"attachment already minted another invoice, then compares the full set of "
"invoice fields the confirm owns before returning an existing same-ID "
"record. A differing re-confirm is refused with divergent field names to "
"avoid duplicate records for one document or silently discarded "
"corrections. It links the source attachment to the invoice, updates the "
"evidence summary where a purchase-evidence record exists, and writes a "
"durable confirmation record on both new and guarded no-op outcomes. The "
"result carries the re-read draft, operator-stamped provenance, "
"establishment summary, confirmation ID and printed-versus-recorded total "
"discrepancy. Candidate field resolution "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) Idempotency "
"and persistence order "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) "
"Prepare/persist boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) Operation "
"write fence and result "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_confirm_operation.py`) "
"Confirmation projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_operation_dtos.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:30
msgid ""
"The operation enters irreversible write custody and marks UNKNOWN before "
"its persistence function; successful completion is UPDATED even when "
"catalogue creation is a no-op, because attachment linking and "
"confirmation audit still occur. However, the local service sequences "
"catalogue creation, manifest link, evidence summary update, and "
"confirmation-record write as distinct calls. Confirm concrete adapter "
"transactions and recovery behavior: a crash after one write but before "
"later writes can leave an incomplete provenance chain, and the "
"attachment's list of already minted invoice IDs is central to the "
"duplicate-document guard. The operation's UNKNOWN effect is conservative,"
" but it does not itself make those stores atomic. Ordered persistence "
"calls (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) Effect "
"boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_confirm_operation.py`) "
"Attachment-based prior-invoice lookup "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:32
msgid "Local reader readiness and implementation assessment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:34
msgid ""
"The readiness operation reports host platform/endpoint facts, runtime "
"reachability, model-role installation/residency/fitness/admission, the "
"last local pull, and whether extraction is ready. It does not load or "
"install a model and it returns no document or tax values. Exact profile "
"binding, metadata access, result bounds, no-effect receipt checks, and "
"CLI/TUI projection are enforced in the operation. Readiness projection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_readiness_operation.py`)"
" Read-only executor "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_readiness_operation.py`)"
" Metadata access policy "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_readiness_operation.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md:36
msgid ""
"The strongest local controls are content-bound review freshness, re-"
"extraction at confirmation, distinct structured/text/vision lanes, "
"refusal to fabricate missing fields, per-finding answers, exact-profile "
"operation checks, and cautious effect accounting. Cross-module "
"verification should focus on concrete reader/consent adapters, token "
"audit coverage across vision and semantic stages, and recovery/atomicity "
"of multi-store confirmation writes. The projections are size-bounded, but"
" the permitted tax-rich result and filesystem/adapter confidentiality "
"remain dependent on the registered access and composition layers. No "
"tests in these files were inspected or run; static inspection cannot "
"verify actual provider routing, cancellation timing, durability, or legal"
" accuracy."
msgstr ""

